1
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:26,000
From 1968 til 1972, twenty-four human beings went to the moon.
Their journey lives as the ultimate adventure story.

2
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:46,000
For All Mankind is a documentary, history film directed by Al Reinert.

3
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
A testament to NASA's Apollo program of the 1960s and '70s.

4
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:26,000
Composed of actual NASA footage of the missions and astronaut interviews, the documentary offers the
viewpoint of the individuals who braved the remarkable journey to the moon and back.

5
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Narrator - Apollo 8, Apollo 13 (voice), played by Jim Lovell.

6
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Narrator - Apollo 9 (voice), played by Russell Schweickart.

7
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:26,000
Narrator - Apollo 10, Apollo 17 (voice), played by Eugene Cernan.

8
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Narrator - Apollo 11 (voice), played by Michael Collins.

9
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Narrator - Apollo 12 (voice), played by Charles Conrad.

10
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
Narrator - Apollo 12 (voice), played by Richard Gordon.

11
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
For All Mankind  is a 1987 documentary film made of original footage from NASA's Apollo program,
which successfully prepared and landed the first humans on the Moon from 1968 to 1972.

12
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
It was directed by Al Reinert, with music by Brian Eno.

13
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
The film, consisting of footage from Apollo 7 through Apollo 17, was assembled to depict what seems like a single trip to the Moon, highlighting
the beauty and otherworldliness of the images by only using audio from the interviews Reinert conducted with Apollo crew members.

14
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
The film explores themes of nasa, space mission, moon
landing, astronaut, space exploration.
